#   * the level prefixes — Error:, Warning:, Notice:, Info:, Crit: — which
#     say how bad it is, not what it says, and which callers read;
#   * anything of the shape name=value or name[0]='value', which is output
#     meant for a program;
#   * option names (--keyservers), action names (certify, print_secret) and
#     property names (FN:, UID:urn:eid:), which are typed, not read;
#   * fingerprints, and the words u4 and u5.
